  "guide.buildcraftreborn.intro.title": "Getting started",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.intro.1": "Welcome to BuildCraft Reborn! Pick a chapter on the left and use the arrows to turn pages. Energy comes from Craft Energy: 1 MJ of the original mod is 1 CWh here, so an engine giving 1 MJ per tick gives 1,000 CW.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.intro.2": "A good path: wooden gears and a wrench, a redstone or Stirling engine, a pump or mining well, then pipes. Later: the quarry, oil and the combustion engine, lasers and chipsets, gates, and finally the builders.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.tools.title": "Tools and markers",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.tools.1": "The wrench turns engines, pumps and many vanilla blocks; on iron, wooden and daizuli pipes it changes the special side. Gears (wood, stone, iron, gold, diamond) are the base of most recipes.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.tools.2": "Land Marks placed in a line connect with a laser when right-clicked; three connected in a corner form a box used by the quarry, filler and architect table. Path Marks build a path for the builder. The paintbrush colours blocks and the list stores item filters.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.engines.title": "Engines",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.engines.1": "Engines push power out of their front face and must be switched on with redstone. The redstone engine gives 50 CW, the Stirling engine burns fuel for 1,000 CW (both at 220 MV) and the combustion engine burns liquid fuels at 1,000 MV.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.engines.2": "The trunk colour shows the heat: blue, green, yellow, red. An overheated engine stops. The combustion engine needs coolant (water or ice) or it will overheat quickly; oil residue collects in its tank.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.factory.title": "Factory",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.factory.1": "The tank stores 16,000 CL and stacks on top of other tanks. The pump drains fluid sources below it and the flood gate fills an area. The mining well digs straight down and sends the blocks to pipes or inventories.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.factory.2": "The auto workbench crafts the recipe in its ghost grid using the materials inside, 40 CWh per item. Machines take power through any side from engines or cables.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.quarry.title": "Quarry and filler",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.quarry.1": "Place the quarry next to a Land Mark box (or it uses an 11 by 11 area behind it). It builds a frame, then mines layer by layer down to bedrock, sending the items to an adjacent pipe or chest. Breaking costs energy based on block hardness.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.quarry.2": "The filler also uses a marker box. Choose a pattern (fill, box, pyramid, stairs, spheres and 2D shapes) and it places blocks from its inventory, clearing what is in the way when Excavate is on.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.pipes.title": "Item pipes",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.pipes.1": "Wooden pipes pull items out of inventories when powered. Cobblestone, stone and quartz pipes do not connect to each other; gold pipes speed items up, iron pipes send everything to one side and diamond pipes sort by the filters set for each side.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.pipes.2": "Clay pipes prefer inventories, void pipes destroy items, obsidian pipes suck up dropped items and sandstone pipes never touch machines. Structure pipes only hold gates and wires.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.fluid_pipes.title": "Fluid pipes",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.fluid_pipes.1": "Combine an item pipe with pipe sealant to make its fluid version. Better materials move more fluid per tick. A wooden fluid pipe pulls from tanks and machines when powered.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.fluid_pipes.2": "Iron fluid pipes choose one output and diamond fluid pipes use fluid containers as filters. Fluid never flows back through the side it entered for a few seconds.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.special_pipes.title": "Special pipes",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.special_pipes.1": "Lazuli pipes paint the items passing through (wrench changes the colour). Daizuli pipes send items of their colour only through the special side. Wooden diamond pipes extract one item at a time using a whitelist, blacklist or round robin; emzuli pipes use four gate-controlled presets.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.special_pipes.2": "Lenses paint items crossing a face and filters only let their colour through. The stripes pipe breaks the block at its tip, uses items there and extends itself with pipe items. Facades cover a pipe face with any full block; the filtered buffer holds one item type per slot.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.oil.title": "Oil and refining",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.oil.1": "Oil wells appear in deserts, badlands and oceans, sometimes with a tall spout. Oil is sticky and burns. Pump it into tanks and burn it in the combustion engine, or refine it for better fuels.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.oil.2": "The distiller splits a hot fluid into a gas that goes up and a liquid that goes down. The heat exchanger (start, middle parts and end) heats one fluid with another. The water gelifier and gelled water help build dams.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.silicon.title": "Lasers and tables",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.silicon.1": "Lasers shoot power into nearby assembly tables and advanced crafting tables. The assembly table makes chipsets, gates, lenses, plugs and wires: mark the recipes you want and it builds them in turn while it has materials.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.silicon.2": "The advanced crafting table crafts its 3 by 3 pattern from the materials inside, powered by lasers. More lasers mean faster crafting.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.gates.title": "Gates and wires",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.gates.1": "Put a gate on a pipe face. Each slot pairs a trigger (redstone, inventory or tank level, engine heat, items in the pipe, timers, light) with an action (redstone output, wire signal, machine off, pulsar, painting). AND gates need every trigger of a group, OR gates just one.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.gates.2": "Pipe wires run along the corners of pipes and carry a signal of their colour between gates. The pulsar powers wooden pipes, the timer and light sensor add triggers, and the gate copier copies settings between gates. Sneak-click removes a plug.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.builders.title": "Builders",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.builders.1": "The architect table scans a marker box into a template (shape only) or a blueprint (exact blocks). Rename the blank item in an anvil to name the scan. The builder places the design behind itself, turned to face like the builder, using materials from its inventory and tanks.",
  "guide.buildcraftreborn.builders.2": "The electronic library stores designs in a folder shared by every world. The replacer swaps one block for another in a blueprint using two single block schematics. Path Marks behind a builder make it build once at every point of the path."
}
